.TH GHSTARS-TUI 5 "2026-08-26" "ghstars 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
ghstars-tui \- TUI configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.ghstars/config/tui.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file uses TOML syntax.
A missing file selects every default.
A present invalid file stops TUI startup with an error.
.PP
Press
.B g
in the TUI to edit this file.
The editor preserves existing comments and key order.
It writes changed settings only after Escape validates the form.
Restart ghstars after a save.
.SH TOP-LEVEL FIELDS
.TP
.B layout
Initial Layout name.
Valid values are
.B compact
and
.BR balanced .
The default is
.BR compact .
.TP
.B header_height
Positive integer table header height.
The default is 1.
.TP
.B show_clock
Boolean that controls the title clock.
The default is false.
.TP
.B date_format
Date format passed to Python
.BR strftime (3).
The default is
.BR %d-%b-%Y .
.TP
.B toast_timeout
Positive integer notification duration in seconds.
The default is 8.
.TP
.B ascii_only
Boolean that replaces status glyphs with text markers.
The default is false.
.TP
.B default_filter
Optional Filter key that applies when TUI state has no Filter.
The default is unset.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
The
.B [keybindings]
table maps an action name to one Textual key string.
The editor shows one row for each action.
.PP
The 17 action names are:
.BR quit ,
.BR tag_selected ,
.BR toggle_detail_pane ,
.BR toggle_select ,
.BR select_all ,
.BR clear_selection ,
.BR show_lists ,
.BR open_filter ,
.BR clear_discovery ,
.BR cycle_layout ,
.BR open_in_browser ,
.BR unstar_selected ,
.BR cycle_sort ,
.BR open_search ,
.BR close_search ,
.BR refresh_rate_limit ,
and
.BR sync .
.PP
The default keys are
.BR q ,
.BR t ,
.BR d ,
.BR space ,
.BR a ,
.BR c ,
.BR l ,
.BR f ,
.BR x ,
.BR z ,
.BR o ,
.BR u ,
.BR s ,
.BR slash ,
.BR escape ,
.BR r ,
and
.BR y
in the same order.
.PP
Keys must be parseable and unique after defaults and overrides merge.
The fixed keys
.BR ctrl+c ,
.BR ctrl+q ,
.BR ctrl+p ,
and
.B g
cannot be used.
.SH CATEGORY COLOURS
The
.B [category_colours]
table maps a Category name to one fixed colour name.
Valid names are
.BR red ,
.BR orange ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR green ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR blue ,
.BR magenta ,
and
.BR violet .
.PP
Example:
.nf
[category_colours]
AI = "magenta"
DevOps = "cyan"
.fi
.SH LAYOUTS
The file can define
.B [layouts.compact]
and
.BR [layouts.balanced] .
A missing preset uses its shipped default.
Each preset supports these fields:
.TP
.B columns
Ordered array of optional table column names.
The Sel and Star columns always appear first.
Valid names are Owner, Language, License, Stars, Starred at, First seen, Membership, Fork, Follow, Archived, Archived at, and Last checked.
.TP
.B detail_pane_visible
Boolean that controls the preset's Detail pane default.
The default is true.
.TP
.B row_height
Positive integer Star row height.
The default is 1.
.TP
.B detail_pane_height
Positive integer Detail pane height.
The default is 14.
.PP
The shipped compact columns are Language, Stars, and Membership.
The shipped balanced columns are Language, Stars, Membership, License, Owner, and Starred at.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
layout = "compact"
header_height = 1
show_clock = false
date_format = "%d-%b-%Y"
toast_timeout = 8
ascii_only = false

[keybindings]
tag_selected = "shift+t"

[category_colours]
AI = "magenta"

[layouts.compact]
columns = ["Language", "Stars", "Membership"]
detail_pane_visible = true
row_height = 1
detail_pane_height = 14
.fi
.SH REMOVED FIELDS
The old
.B [colours]
table is invalid.
The TUI uses the active Textual theme.
.SH STATE FILE
Do not put session state in this file.
The machine-owned
.I ~/.ghstars/state/tui-state.toml
stores the active Layout, sort, Filter, and Detail pane override.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ghstars (1),
.BR ghstars-tui (1)
